      dealing: 'One hole card face down to each player. Then the dealer offers one card face up to the player to his left; that player may accept it or pay the agreed price to push it and receive the next card from the deck (second card must be accepted). The next player is offered the pushed card or a new card; this continues for all players. After each of four such rounds there is a betting round. Final hand is five cards (one hole, four up); highest hand wins.',
