    turnFlow: "After one hole card each, the dealer offers one card face up to the player to his left. That player may accept it or pay the agreed price to push it and receive the next card from the deck (must accept the second). The next player is offered the pushed card if the previous player pushed, otherwise a new card; same accept-or-push choice. This continues until all have received a card; any card pushed by the last player is discarded. Betting round begins with the player showing the highest hand. Three more rounds of offering and pushing (each starting with a fresh card to the first active player to dealer's left), each followed by a betting round. After the fourth round all active players have five cards (four face up). Showdown: highest hand wins.",
